{
  "answer": "GET /admin/reports/latency → ReportsController.latency → ReportsService.latency → ReportsRepository.findLatency → ClickHouseService.query.\n\n1. ReportsController.latency receives LatencyQueryDto and calls this.reports.latency(query).\n2. ReportsService.latency resolves query.from/query.to with resolveTimeRange, then calls this.reportsRepository.findLatency(range, query.limit, query.endpoint).\n3. ReportsRepository.findLatency calls this.clickhouse.query<LatencyRow> with parameterized SQL against endpoint_latency_stats. It filters minute within [from, to), optionally filters endpoint, groups by endpoint and method, merges request counts and average/percentile latency states, orders by p95Ms descending, and applies limit.\n4. ClickHouseService.query executes client.query with the SQL, query_params, and JSONEachRow format, then returns parsed rows.\n\nThe service wraps the rows as { data, meta: { from, to } }; the controller returns that report or CSV when requested.",
